1
00:00:07,910 --> 00:00:14,900
A basketball coach records the points scored by two teams in 12 matches each: the Hawks and the Owls.

2
00:00:14,950 --> 00:00:18,800
She wants one diagram that shows both, in order.

3
00:00:18,850 --> 00:00:25,170
Which diagram can show two sets of data: a back-to-back stem-and-leaf diagram, or a pie chart?

4
00:00:25,220 --> 00:00:28,400
Pause the video and choose.

5
00:00:28,450 --> 00:00:31,460
A back-to-back stem-and-leaf diagram.

6
00:00:31,510 --> 00:00:39,380
Remember: in a stem-and-leaf diagram, the stems are the tens and the leaves are the units, in order, with a key.

7
00:00:39,430 --> 00:00:41,850
Both teams share one column of stems.

8
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:44,130
The Hawks' leaves go to the right.

9
00:00:44,180 --> 00:00:46,270
The Owls' leaves go to the left.

10
00:00:46,320 --> 00:00:50,300
Each side is in order, going outwards from the stem.

11
00:00:50,350 --> 00:00:50,980
Your turn.

12
00:00:51,030 --> 00:00:53,230
What was the Hawks' lowest score?

13
00:00:53,280 --> 00:00:56,460
Pause the video and try it.

14
00:00:56,510 --> 00:00:59,100
Stem 3, leaf 4: 34.

15
00:00:59,150 --> 00:01:05,100
The Hawks' median is the mean of the 6th and 7th values, 46 and 49.

16
00:01:05,150 --> 00:01:06,270
That is 47.5.

17
00:01:06,320 --> 00:01:10,400
Their range is 64 minus 34, which is 30.

18
00:01:10,450 --> 00:01:11,780
Here is the method.

19
00:01:11,830 --> 00:01:14,800
Step 1: write one column of stems.

20
00:01:14,850 --> 00:01:20,290
Step 2: put one set on the right, and one on the left, in order outwards.

21
00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:23,140
Step 3: add a key for each side.

22
00:01:23,190 --> 00:01:26,510
Step 4: compare the medians and ranges.

23
00:01:26,560 --> 00:01:29,910
On the left, read stem then leaf.

24
00:01:29,960 --> 00:01:38,800
The Owls' scores are 32, 36, 39, then 40, 41, 42, 44, 47, then 53, 55, 58 and 60.

25
00:01:38,850 --> 00:01:41,710
5 Owls scores were in the forties.

26
00:01:41,760 --> 00:01:45,690
Their range is 60 minus 32, which is 28.

27
00:01:45,740 --> 00:01:46,370
Your turn.

28
00:01:46,420 --> 00:01:48,080
What is the Owls' median?

29
00:01:48,130 --> 00:01:50,980
Pause and work it out.

30
00:01:51,030 --> 00:01:54,460
The 6th and 7th values are 42 and 44.

31
00:01:54,510 --> 00:01:56,610
The median is 43.

32
00:01:56,660 --> 00:01:59,360
Now compare the medians and the ranges.

33
00:01:59,410 --> 00:02:05,360
The Owls were a little more consistent, with a smaller range: 28, against 30.

34
00:02:05,410 --> 00:02:10,870
On the Owls' side, stem 3 shows the leaves 9, 6, 2, with 2 next to the stem.

35
00:02:10,920 --> 00:02:11,810
Dev reads it.

36
00:02:11,860 --> 00:02:13,810
Which line is wrong?

37
00:02:13,860 --> 00:02:14,910
Line 1 is wrong.

38
00:02:14,960 --> 00:02:19,050
Left leaves get bigger going outwards from the stem.

39
00:02:19,100 --> 00:02:21,920
The values are 32, 36 and 39.

40
00:02:21,970 --> 00:02:24,350
The smallest is 32.

41
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:33,130
Doctors and sports scientists use back-to-back diagrams to compare two groups, like results before and after training.

42
00:02:33,180 --> 00:02:34,330
One last question.

43
00:02:34,380 --> 00:02:38,140
Which team has the higher median: the Hawks, or the Owls?

44
00:02:38,190 --> 00:02:41,340
Pause the video and choose.

45
00:02:41,390 --> 00:02:45,470
The Hawks, with 47.5, compared with 43.

46
00:02:45,520 --> 00:02:50,060
To remember: one column of stems, with leaves on both sides.

47
00:02:50,110 --> 00:02:53,060
Order the leaves outwards from the stem.

48
00:02:53,110 --> 00:02:55,420
Give a key for each side.

49
00:02:55,470 --> 00:02:57,930
Compare medians and ranges.

50
00:02:57,980 --> 00:03:03,390
Great work! Now practise lesson 15.3 on Camday.
